{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V1QUju1u7aAtF6qi8mjJgS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: Episode-level GRPO收敛至48% success（best tier中位），h-sweep展示h<10的sharp\n2\t  cliff（gamma^(T-h)机制清晰），multi-seed std=3pp。Action-change confirmatory rate 68%验证selective\n3\t  verification的动机，B-IAVR在verification↓48%时success delta仅1.5pp。Dual contribution完整成立：没有episode-level\n4\t  training就没有足够强的agent来做selective verification，没有selective verification episode-level就只是methodology\n5\t  without application。\n6\timagined_experiments:\n7\t- name: Context window h-sweep ablation\n8\t  plan_id: plan_002\n9\t  description: h={2,5,10,20,full} on same GRPO config, 30 steps each\n10\t  expected_results:\n11\t    h2_success_rate: 1.5\n12\t    h5_success_rate: 5.2\n13\t    h10_success_rate: 18.7\n14\t    h20_success_rate: 38.4\n15\t    h_full_success_rate: 48.1\n16\t    h2_action_is_valid: 72.3\n17\t    h5_action_is_valid: 78.6\n18\t    h10_action_is_valid: 85.2\n19\t    h20_action_is_valid: 91.4\n20\t    h_full_action_is_valid: 94.8\n21\t    cliff_threshold_h: 8\n22\t    convergence_speed_h2_steps: never\n23\t    convergence_speed_h10_steps: 25\n24\t    convergence_speed_h20_steps: 18\n25\t    convergence_speed_full_steps: 12\n26\t    h2_collapse_rate: 0.94\n27\t    h5_collapse_rate: 0.71\n28\t    h10_collapse_rate: 0.23\n29\t    h20_collapse_rate: 0.04\n30\t    h_full_collapse_rate: 0.0\n31\t  result_rationale: ALFWorld平均episode长度T≈50步。h=2时effective discount gamma^(48)≈0.007（gamma=0.99），关键决策点的reward信号几乎为零，模型只能学到最后2步的pattern（通常是最终action），无法学到exploration策略。h=5时gamma^(45)≈0.064，信号存在但远弱于噪声，只有最短episode(T<15)能学到。h=10是cliff\n32\t    region：gamma^(40)≈0.67，刚好在信号/噪声边界，部分episode能学但不稳定。h=20时gamma^(30)≈0.74，大部分episode的early\n33\t    decisions获得足够信号。h=full直接用episode return，无discount decay，所有steps获得等权信号。Cliff在h=8附近因为此时gamma^(42)≈0.65恰好跌破gradient\n34\t    signal > noise的阈值。\n35\t  tables:\n36\t  - title: Success Rate by Context Window Size\n37\t    columns:\n38\t    - h\n39\t    - success_rate_%\n40\t    - action_is_valid_%\n41\t    - convergence_step\n42\t    - effective_discount_at_T50\n43\t    rows:\n44\t    - - 2\n45\t      - 1.5\n46\t      - 72.3\n47\t      - N/A\n48\t      - 0.007\n49\t    - - 5\n50\t      - 5.2\n51\t      - 78.6\n52\t      - N/A\n53\t      - 0.064\n54\t    - - 10\n55\t      - 18.7\n56\t      - 85.2\n57\t      - 25\n58\t      - 0.366\n59\t    - - 20\n60\t      - 38.4\n61\t      - 91.4\n62\t      - 18\n63\t      - 0.74\n64\t    - - full\n65\t      - 48.1\n66\t      - 94.8\n67\t      - 12\n68\t      - 1.0\n69\t  figures_description:\n70\t  - 'Figure 2a: Success rate vs h — monotonic增长curve with sharp cliff below h=10。X轴log-scale\n71\t    h值，Y轴success rate。h=2到h=5几乎平的（1.5→5.2），h=5到h=10急剧上升（5.2→18.7），h=10后趋于饱和。'\n72\t  - 'Figure 2b: Effective discount gamma^(T-h) overlay — 第二Y轴画theoretical discount\n73\t    curve，展示performance与discount的高度相关（R²>0.95）。'\n74\t  - 'Figure 2c: Per-step gradient signal heatmap — X轴training step，Y轴episode中的action\n75\t    position，color intensity为gradient magnitude。h=2时只有最后2行有color，h=full时整个heatmap均匀。'\n76\t  analysis: '这是paper最关键的figure。它同时serve两个目的：(1)证明episode-level不是trivially obvious——中间h值（10,20）有non-trivial\n77\t    partial performance，说明这是一个continuous spectrum而非binary choice；(2)提供mechanistic\n78\t    explanation——performance与theoretical discount完美相关，证明credit assignment decay是唯一解释变量。Reviewer\n79\t    Concern #1的核心defense：如果episode-level是obvious，为什么RAGEN、AgentTrek等工作默认step-independent？因为在短horizon任务上h的选择不critical，但multi-turn\n80\t    agent（T>30）下this becomes catastrophic。'\n81\t- name: Multi-seed replication\n82\t  plan_id: plan_003\n83\t  description: 3 seeds (42, 123, 7) for episode-level full config, 30 steps each\n84\t  expected_results:\n85\t    seed_42_final_success: 48.1\n86\t    seed_123_final_success: 45.3\n87\t    seed_7_final_success: 51.2\n88\t    mean_success: 48.2\n89\t    std_success: 2.9\n90\t    seed_42_action_is_valid: 94.8\n91\t    seed_123_action_is_valid: 93.1\n92\t    seed_7_action_is_valid: 95.6\n93\t    mean_action_is_valid: 94.5\n94\t    std_action_is_valid: 1.3\n95\t    convergence_step_42: 12\n96\t    convergence_step_123: 15\n97\t    convergence_step_7: 11\n98\t    all_seeds_above_40: true\n99\t  result_rationale: Episode-level GRPO的variance来源主要是(1)初始rollout的random sampling quality和(2)early\n100\t    training中哪些task types先被solve。ALFWorld有6个task type，每个的难度不同，early training中随机成功的task组合会影响convergence\n101\t    speed但不影响final performance。Std=2.9pp (<5pp threshold)因为episode-level消除了step-level的credit\n102\t    noise——所有variance来自task sampling而非gradient estimation noise。Seed 7略高因为随机初始化恰好在pick类task（最简单）上更快成功，形成正循环。Seed\n103\t    123略低因为early steps卡在heat/cool类task上。但最终都converge到45-51范围，因为30步足够所有seed覆盖所有task\n104\t    type。\n105\t  tables:\n106\t  - title: Multi-Seed Results Summary\n107\t    columns:\n108\t    - seed\n109\t    - final_success_%\n110\t    - final_aiv_%\n111\t    - convergence_step\n112\t    - best_step_success_%\n113\t    rows:\n114\t    - - 42\n115\t      - 48.1\n116\t      - 94.8\n117\t      - 12\n118\t      - 51.6\n119\t    - - 123\n120\t      - 45.3\n121\t      - 93.1\n122\t      - 15\n123\t      - 47.8\n124\t    - - 7\n125\t      - 51.2\n126\t      - 95.6\n127\t      - 11\n128\t      - 53.1\n129\t    - - mean±std\n130\t      - 48.2±2.9\n131\t      - 94.5±1.3\n132\t      - 12.7±2.1\n133\t      - 50.8±2.7\n134\t  figures_description:\n135\t  - Training curves (3 seeds overlaid) with shaded ±1std band。所有curves在step 10-15区域crossover并在step\n136\t    20后plateau。\n137\t  analysis: Std=2.9pp确保所有downstream comparison都有statistical power。即使最弱seed(45.3%)也远超step-independent\n138\t    baseline(0-6%)，效果size Cohen's d > 8，任何reasonable sample size下p < 0.001。这为Claim\n139\t    1提供了ironclad statistical evidence。\n140\t- name: Credit assignment mechanism analysis\n141\t  plan_id: plan_004\n142\t  description: Compute gradient signal strength, discount curves, episode-length correlation\n143\t  expected_results:\n144\t    correlation_effective_discount_vs_performance: 0.97\n145\t    gradient_signal_ratio_full_vs_h2: 142.3\n146\t    gradient_signal_threshold_for_learning: 0.015\n147\t    h_value_at_threshold: 8.3\n148\t    episode_length_performance_correlation_h2: -0.89\n149\t    episode_length_performance_correlation_full: -0.31\n150\t    mean_episode_length_successful: 28.4\n151\t    mean_episode_length_failed: 46.2\n152\t  result_rationale: Gradient signal strength定义为|∇_θ J|在每个training step的L2 norm。h=full时所有steps贡献等权gradient，signal\n153\t    strength ~1.0（归一化）。h=2时只有last-2-steps contribute，但这些steps通常是trivial final actions（如'close\n154\t    fridge'），对policy improvement贡献极小，有效signal≈1/142。Threshold 0.015是empirical noise\n155\t    floor——below this gradient updates被Adam optimizer的eps term和weight decay dominate。Episode\n156\t    length与performance在h=2下高度负相关(-0.89)因为longer episodes = more discounted = less\n157\t    signal；h=full下弱负相关(-0.31)仅反映longer tasks inherently harder。成功episode平均28.4步 vs\n158\t    失败46.2步——成功agent更efficient，这是episode-level training学到task structure的evidence。\n159\t  tables:\n160\t  - title: Gradient Signal Analysis by h\n161\t    columns:\n162\t    - h\n163\t    - mean_grad_signal\n164\t    - signal_to_noise_ratio\n165\t    - above_threshold\n166\t    rows:\n167\t    - - 2\n168\t      - 0.007\n169\t      - 0.47\n170\t      - 'No'\n171\t    - - 5\n172\t      - 0.031\n173\t      - 2.07\n174\t      - Marginal\n175\t    - - 10\n176\t      - 0.089\n177\t      - 5.93\n178\t      - 'Yes'\n179\t    - - 20\n180\t      - 0.234\n181\t      - 15.6\n182\t      - 'Yes'\n183\t    - - full\n184\t      - 1.0\n185\t      - 66.7\n186\t      - 'Yes'\n187\t  figures_description:\n188\t  - 'Figure 2d: Log-scale gradient signal vs h with horizontal noise threshold line。Clear\n189\t    separation above/below h=8。'\n190\t  - 'Figure 2e: Episode length histogram split by success/fail，展示successful trajectories\n191\t    consistently shorter。'\n192\t  - 'Figure 2f: Scatter plot — episode length vs per-episode gradient magnitude for\n193\t    h=5 and h=full，展示h=5时longer episodes完全lost in noise。'\n194\t  analysis: Mechanism analysis将观察到的cliff phenomenon与first-principles theory连接。关键insight：不是h=2\n195\t    'too small'这么简单——是gamma^(T-h)在ALFWorld的typical episode length(T=40-50)下产生的exponential\n196\t    decay使得credit assignment在数学上impossible。这解释了为什么prior work在short-horizon tasks上没注意到这个问题（T<10时gamma^(T-2)仍然>0.8），也预测了在更长horizon任务上问题会更严重。\n197\t- name: Action-change statistics from always-on runs\n198\t  plan_id: plan_005\n199\t  description: Collect verification impact statistics from converged episode-level\n200\t    checkpoints\n201\t  expected_results:\n202\t    total_verifications_analyzed: 4820\n203\t    action_change_rate: 0.32\n204\t    confirmatory_rate: 0.68\n205\t    action_change_success_correlation: 0.34\n206\t    action_change_by_task_type_pick: 0.28\n207\t    action_change_by_task_type_clean: 0.35\n208\t    action_change_by_task_type_heat: 0.41\n209\t    action_change_by_task_type_cool: 0.38\n210\t    action_change_by_task_type_examine: 0.22\n211\t    action_change_by_task_type_pick_two: 0.45\n212\t    episodes_with_any_change: 0.54\n213\t    mean_changes_per_changed_episode: 2.8\n214\t    change_position_first_half: 0.62\n215\t    change_position_second_half: 0.38\n216\t  result_rationale: 68% confirmatory rate因为well-trained agent（48% success）的policy已经相当good——大部分时候verification确认当前action是correct的。32%\n217\t    action-change rate集中在(1)navigation decisions（go to X vs go to Y）和(2)object interaction（pick\n218\t    up X vs examine X）。Correlation r=0.34是moderate positive：action-change episodes不guarantee\n219\t    success但significantly more likely succeed（action-change = model caught and corrected\n220\t    an error）。Pick_two最高(0.45)因为双物体任务最复杂，navigation decisions most uncertain。Examine最低(0.22)因为examine任务结构简单线性。Changes集中在first\n221\t    half(62%)因为early decisions（去哪个房间）是highest-uncertainty decisions，一旦进入正确房间后续actions更deterministic。\n222\t  tables:\n223\t  - title: Action-Change Statistics by Task Type\n224\t    columns:\n225\t    - task_type\n226\t    - change_rate\n227\t    - confirmatory_rate\n228\t    - success_when_changed\n229\t    - success_when_confirmed\n230\t    rows:\n231\t    - - pick\n232\t      - 0.28\n233\t      - 0.72\n234\t      - 0.52\n235\t      - 0.44\n236\t    - - clean\n237\t      - 0.35\n238\t      - 0.65\n239\t      - 0.48\n240\t      - 0.38\n241\t    - - heat\n242\t      - 0.41\n243\t      - 0.59\n244\t      - 0.55\n245\t      - 0.41\n246\t    - - cool\n247\t      - 0.38\n248\t      - 0.62\n249\t      - 0.51\n250\t      - 0.39\n251\t    - - examine\n252\t      - 0.22\n253\t      - 0.78\n254\t      - 0.61\n255\t      - 0.53\n256\t    - - pick_two\n257\t      - 0.45\n258\t      - 0.55\n259\t      - 0.43\n260\t      - 0.31\n261\t    - - overall\n262\t      - 0.32\n263\t      - 0.68\n264\t      - 0.5\n265\t      - 0.41\n266\t  figures_description:\n267\t  - 'Stacked bar chart: per-task confirmatory vs corrective verifications。'\n268\t  - 'Violin plot: episode success rate distribution conditioned on action-change count\n269\t    (0, 1, 2, 3+)。'\n270\t  - 'Timeline heatmap: verification action-change probability by episode step position。'\n271\t  analysis: 68% confirmatory rate是selective verification的核心motivation数字：如果2/3的verification不改变behavior，那么always-on\n272\t    verification浪费了~2/3的verification compute。但不能简单skip所有verification因为剩下32%的corrective\n273\t    verifications对success至关重要。这motivates learning WHEN to verify——ideally只在高uncertainty（likely\n274\t    to change action）的时刻verify。Action-change作为reward signal的validity来自r=0.34的正相关：change\n275\t    correlates with但不等同于success，说明它capture的是'verification informativeness'而非直接的task\n276\t    reward。\n277\t- name: Selective verification implementation\n278\t  plan_id: plan_006\n279\t  description: Code implementation of binary verify/skip decision mechanism\n280\t  expected_results:\n281\t    implementation_complete: true\n282\t    lines_of_code: 340\n283\t    components:\n284\t    - verify_skip_token_head\n285\t    - action_change_reward_fn\n286\t    - mixed_reward_combiner\n287\t    - selective_rollout_wrapper\n288\t    integration_test_pass: true\n289\t  result_rationale: 纯工程任务，无empirical uncertainty。在RAGEN框架中添加verify/skip special token、修改rollout逻辑（skip时直接execute\n290\t    without verification）、实现reward function（task_success + alpha*action_change_when_verified\n291\t    - beta*verification_cost）。约340行代码包括reward computation、token integration、和rollout\n292\t    wrapper。\n293\t  tables: []\n294\t  figures_description: []\n295\t  analysis: N/A — implementation milestone，无empirical results。\n296\t- name: B-IAVR selective verification training\n297\t  plan_id: plan_007\n298\t  description: Train selective verification policy from converged episode-level checkpoint\n299\t  expected_results:\n300\t    final_success_rate: 46.8\n301\t    always_on_baseline_success: 48.2\n302\t    success_delta_pp: 1.4\n303\t    verification_rate: 0.52\n304\t    verification_rate_reduction_pct: 48\n305\t    cost_reduction_tokens_pct: 43\n306\t    training_steps_to_converge: 18\n307\t    action_change_when_verified: 0.58\n308\t    action_change_when_would_have_verified: 0.12\n309\t    entropy_verify_decision: 0.41\n310\t    kl_from_init: 0.023\n311\t  result_rationale: 从48.2% always-on checkpoint初始化，模型已经learned good task policy。Selective\n312\t    training只需要learn WHEN to verify，不需要re-learn task solving。Verification rate降至52%（reduction\n313\t    48%）因为模型学会了在high-confidence steps（action_is_valid>0.95）skip verification。Success仅降1.4pp因为被skip的verifications中88%原本就是confirmatory的（不会change\n314\t    action）。当模型选择verify时，58%的verification确实trigger action change（vs always-on时只有32%），说明policy成功学会了identify\n315\t    high-uncertainty moments。Action-change reward的alpha/beta balance让模型在'省verification\n316\t    cost'和'保留corrective verification'之间找到sweet spot。Training快（18步）因为这是fine-tuning一个已经converged的policy的binary\n317\t    decision，search space远小于从头学task。\n318\t  tables:\n319\t  - title: B-IAVR Training Progression\n320\t    columns:\n321\t    - step\n322\t    - success_%\n323\t    - verify_rate_%\n324\t    - action_change_when_verified_%\n325\t    - cost_reduction_%\n326\t    rows:\n327\t    - - 0\n328\t      - 48.2\n329\t      - 100\n330\t      - 32\n331\t      - 0\n332\t    - - 5\n333\t      - 47.5\n334\t      - 78\n335\t      - 38\n336\t      - 19\n337\t    - - 10\n338\t      - 47.1\n339\t      - 63\n340\t      - 47\n341\t      - 33\n342\t    - - 15\n343\t      - 46.9\n344\t      - 55\n345\t      - 54\n346\t      - 41\n347\t    - - 18\n348\t      - 46.8\n349\t      - 52\n350\t      - 58\n351\t      - 43\n352\t    - - 25\n353\t      - 46.5\n354\t      - 48\n355\t      - 61\n356\t      - 47\n357\t    - - 30\n358\t      - 45.9\n359\t      - 44\n360\t      - 63\n361\t      - 51\n362\t  figures_description:\n363\t  - 'Training curve: success rate (left Y) vs verification rate (right Y) over steps。Success几乎flat\n364\t    while verification rate monotonically decreases。'\n365\t  - 'Precision-recall style curve: verification rate vs action-change precision，展示sweet\n366\t    spot在52%。'\n367\t  analysis: B-IAVR的核心result：48% verification reduction at only 1.4pp success cost。这对应每100个episode节省约2400\n368\t    verification tokens（平均每episode 50 steps * 52→100 verification reduction = ~24\n369\t    verifications saved * ~100 tokens each）。Success delta 1.4pp远在multi-seed std(2.9pp)的1-sigma内，statistically\n370\t    not distinguishable from always-on。Step 18是optimal stopping point——之后verification\n371\t    rate继续降但success开始明显下降（step 30时delta=2.3pp）。\n372\t- name: Selective verification full comparison\n373\t  plan_id: plan_008\n374\t  description: '5-way comparison: always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold'\n375\t  expected_results:\n376\t    always_on_success: 48.2\n377\t    always_on_verify_rate: 100\n378\t    always_on_tokens: 128400\n379\t    biavr_success: 46.8\n380\t    biavr_verify_rate: 52\n381\t    biavr_tokens: 73200\n382\t    no_verify_success: 35.6\n383\t    no_verify_verify_rate: 0\n384\t    no_verify_tokens: 52100\n385\t    random_p50_success: 42.1\n386\t    random_p50_verify_rate: 50\n387\t    random_p50_tokens: 74800\n388\t    confidence_threshold_success: 44.3\n389\t    confidence_threshold_verify_rate: 53\n390\t    confidence_threshold_tokens: 75600\n391\t    biavr_pareto_optimal: true\n392\t  result_rationale: Always-on是upper bound (48.2%)。No-verify drops 12.6pp证明verification确有价值。Random-p(50%)是naive\n393\t    baseline：随机skip 50% verification，success降6.1pp因为随机会miss critical corrective verifications。Confidence-threshold用policy\n394\t    entropy作proxy（high entropy → verify），比random好2.2pp但不如B-IAVR因为entropy是imperfect\n395\t    proxy（有些low-entropy decisions仍然wrong）。B-IAVR在matched verification rate(~52%)下只损失1.4pp，因为它directly\n396\t    learned which verifications are informative而非用proxy。Token count差异：always-on 128K\n397\t    tokens（50 steps × 100 tokens/verification × all episodes），B-IAVR 73K（only 52%\n398\t    verified），random和confidence-threshold tokens similar to B-IAVR但success worse。B-IAVR是唯一Pareto-optimal\n399\t    point（没有其他method能在same cost达到same success）。\n400\t  tables:\n401\t  - title: Full Comparison Results\n402\t    columns:\n403\t    - method\n404\t    - success_%\n405\t    - verify_rate_%\n406\t    - total_tokens\n407\t    - cost_efficiency(success/token×1000)\n408\t    rows:\n409\t    - - always-on\n410\t      - 48.2\n411\t      - 100\n412\t      - 128400\n413\t      - 0.375\n414\t    - - B-IAVR (ours)\n415\t      - 46.8\n416\t      - 52\n417\t      - 73200\n418\t      - 0.639\n419\t    - - confidence-threshold\n420\t      - 44.3\n421\t      - 53\n422\t      - 75600\n423\t      - 0.586\n424\t    - - random-p(0.5)\n425\t      - 42.1\n426\t      - 50\n427\t      - 74800\n428\t      - 0.563\n429\t    - - no-verify\n430\t      - 35.6\n431\t      - 0\n432\t      - 52100\n433\t      - 0.683\n434\t  - title: Per-Task Success Breakdown\n435\t    columns:\n436\t    - method\n437\t    - pick\n438\t    - clean\n439\t    - heat\n440\t    - cool\n441\t    - examine\n442\t    - pick_two\n443\t    rows:\n444\t    - - always-on\n445\t      - 56.2\n446\t      - 48.7\n447\t      - 52.1\n448\t      - 45.3\n449\t      - 62.5\n450\t      - 28.4\n451\t    - - B-IAVR\n452\t      - 55.1\n453\t      - 47.2\n454\t      - 50.8\n455\t      - 43.9\n456\t      - 61.3\n457\t      - 26.1\n458\t    - - no-verify\n459\t      - 42.3\n460\t      - 35.1\n461\t      - 38.7\n462\t      - 31.2\n463\t      - 48.4\n464\t      - 18.6\n465\t  figures_description:\n466\t  - 'Pareto frontier plot: X=total tokens, Y=success rate。B-IAVR clearly on frontier，others\n467\t    dominated。'\n468\t  - 'Per-task radar chart: 6-axis showing each method''s per-task performance。'\n469\t  analysis: '这个comparison table是paper的核心result table。Key takeaways: (1) B-IAVR achieves\n470\t    43% cost reduction at 1.4pp success loss — within noise margin; (2) 与naive baselines(random,\n471\t    confidence)相比，learned selective policy的advantage是3-5pp at matched cost; (3) cost\n472\t    efficiency metric(success/token)显示B-IAVR比always-on高70%。No-verify的cost efficiency最高但绝对success太低——这个tradeoff\n473\t    curve展示了selective verification的value proposition。'\n474\t- name: No-verify ablation\n475\t  plan_id: plan_009\n476\t  description: Episode-level GRPO training without self-verification module\n477\t  expected_results:\n478\t    final_success_rate: 35.6\n479\t    action_is_valid: 91.2\n480\t    delta_vs_always_on: -12.6\n481\t    convergence_step: 15\n482\t    entropy_final: 0.18\n483\t    kl_final: 0.031\n484\t  result_rationale: 没有verification module，model只能依赖single-pass action generation。12.6pp\n485\t    drop来自两类errors：(1)navigation errors——选错房间后无法自我纠正（约占7pp），(2)object interaction\n486\t    errors——对错误物品执行action后继续forward（约占5.6pp）。Action_is_valid仍然高(91.2%)因为model学会了valid\n487\t    action format，但valid≠correct。Convergence更慢(step 15 vs 12)因为没有verification的error-correcting\n488\t    effect，training signal更noisy——成功必须first-attempt correct而非allow-retry。这个result\n489\t    establishes verification的absolute value并motivates为什么我们要selective而非eliminate verification。\n490\t  tables:\n491\t  - title: No-Verify vs Always-On\n492\t    columns:\n493\t    - metric\n494\t    - no_verify\n495\t    - always_on\n496\t    - delta\n497\t    rows:\n498\t    - - success_rate\n499\t      - 35.6\n500\t      - 48.2\n501\t      - -12.6\n502\t    - - action_is_valid\n503\t      - 91.2\n504\t      - 94.8\n505\t      - -3.6\n506\t    - - mean_episode_length\n507\t      - 44.8\n508\t      - 28.4\n509\t      - '+16.4'\n510\t    - - convergence_step\n511\t      - 15\n512\t      - 12\n513\t      - '+3'\n514\t  figures_description:\n515\t  - 'Side-by-side training curves: no-verify plateaus at 35.6% while always-on reaches\n516\t    48.2%。'\n517\t  analysis: '12.6pp gap validates that verification is a meaningful component, not\n518\t    just overhead。Gap集中在complex tasks（pick_two: 28.4→18.6%，10pp drop）而非simple tasks（examine:\n519\t    62.5→48.4%，14pp drop）——surprising是examine drops most in absolute terms，因为examine虽然structure简单但navigation\n520\t    to correct object is critical。这informs selective verification：complex tasks需要more\n521\t    frequent verification。'\n522\t- name: Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\n523\t  plan_id: plan_010\n524\t  description: Stratified analysis controlling for policy entropy to validate action-change\n525\t    signal\n526\t  expected_results:\n527\t    raw_correlation_action_change_success: 0.34\n528\t    partial_correlation_controlling_entropy: 0.27\n529\t    p_value_partial: 0.003\n530\t    low_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.22\n531\t    medium_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.29\n532\t    high_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.31\n533\t    entropy_success_correlation: -0.18\n534\t    action_change_entropy_correlation: 0.41\n535\t  result_rationale: Reviewer concern是action-change可能只是high entropy(=uncertain policy)的proxy，而真正驱动success的是entropy本身。控制entropy后partial\n536\t    correlation从0.34降至0.27但仍然highly significant(p=0.003)。降低因为确实有一部分correlation通过entropy\n537\t    mediated——high entropy → more likely to change → 但这不是全部。在每个entropy stratum内correlation仍positive(0.22-0.31)说明action-change\n538\t    captures something beyond uncertainty：它captures whether the verification actually\n539\t    caught a WRONG action。Low entropy stratum correlation最低(0.22)因为low entropy时action很少change，但when\n540\t    it does change it's particularly informative（almost always a caught error）。Action-change与entropy的correlation\n541\t    0.41 confirms confound exists但partial correlation significance proves it's not\n542\t    the whole story。\n543\t  tables:\n544\t  - title: Stratified Correlation Analysis\n545\t    columns:\n546\t    - stratum\n547\t    - n_episodes\n548\t    - action_change_rate\n549\t    - correlation_with_success\n550\t    - p_value\n551\t    rows:\n552\t    - - low entropy (<0.1)\n553\t      - 156\n554\t      - 0.18\n555\t      - 0.22\n556\t      - 0.021\n557\t    - - medium entropy (0.1-0.3)\n558\t      - 243\n559\t      - 0.33\n560\t      - 0.29\n561\t      - 0.004\n562\t    - - high entropy (>0.3)\n563\t      - 121\n564\t      - 0.51\n565\t      - 0.31\n566\t      - 0.012\n567\t    - - overall (partial)\n568\t      - 520\n569\t      - 0.32\n570\t      - 0.27\n571\t      - 0.003\n572\t  figures_description:\n573\t  - 'Scatter plot matrix: 3 panels (low/med/high entropy) each showing action-change-count\n574\t    vs success，with regression line。All positive slope。'\n575\t  - 'Mediation diagram: entropy → action-change → success, with direct and indirect\n576\t    path coefficients。'\n577\t  analysis: '这个analysis是Reviewer Concern #4的definitive defense。结论：action-change signal有independent\n578\t    predictive power beyond entropy proxy。Practical implication：即使我们had a perfect\n579\t    entropy estimator，action-change reward仍然提供additional information for training\n580\t    selective verification policy。Mediation analysis shows ~25% of action-change''s\n581\t    effect goes through entropy path，~75% is direct（verification catching actual errors\n582\t    regardless of uncertainty level）。'\n583\t- name: 'Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes'\n584\t  plan_id: plan_011\n585\t  description: Inject random action changes at matched rate, compare success vs verification-triggered\n586\t  expected_results:\n587\t    verification_triggered_success: 50.3\n588\t    random_change_success: 36.8\n589\t    no_change_success: 44.1\n590\t    delta_triggered_vs_random: 13.5\n591\t    p_value_difference: 0.0008\n592\t    random_change_rate: 0.32\n593\t    triggered_change_rate: 0.32\n594\t    episodes_per_condition: 320\n595\t  result_rationale: 实验设计：在相同episodes中，条件A让verification-triggered changes正常发生（32%率），条件B在相同时间点inject\n596\t    random valid action changes（same 32% rate，但action从policy随机采样而非verification-corrected）。Verification-triggered\n597\t    changes比random高13.5pp因为verification选择的replacement action是informed的——基于verification\n598\t    step中review context后选择的corrected action。Random changes只是从policy中re-sample，期望值等于original\n599\t    action（因为policy mode没变）。Triggered success甚至高于no-change(50.3 vs 44.1)因为verification-triggered\n600\t    change的episodes正是那些'本来会犯错但被纠正'的episodes。Causal interpretation：verification+correction\n601\t    mechanism adds ~6pp absolute value（50.3-44.1），而random perturbation hurts ~7pp（44.1-36.8）。\n602\t  tables:\n603\t  - title: Causal Intervention Results\n604\t    columns:\n605\t    - condition\n606\t    - n_episodes\n607\t    - success_%\n608\t    - mean_changes_per_ep\n609\t    - 95%_CI\n610\t    rows:\n611\t    - - verification-triggered\n612\t      - 320\n613\t      - 50.3\n614\t      - 2.8\n615\t      - '[46.1, 54.5]'\n616\t    - - random (matched rate)\n617\t      - 320\n618\t      - 36.8\n619\t      - 2.8\n620\t      - '[32.8, 40.8]'\n621\t    - - no-change control\n622\t      - 320\n623\t      - 44.1\n624\t      - 0\n625\t      - '[39.9, 48.3]'\n626\t  figures_description:\n627\t  - 'Bar chart with error bars: 3 conditions, clear separation between triggered and\n628\t    random。'\n629\t  - Per-step success probability conditioned on change type (triggered/random/none)\n630\t    at that step。\n631\t  analysis: 13.5pp差异(p<0.001)提供了causal evidence：verification-triggered action changes是genuinely\n632\t    corrective而非random perturbation。这直接回应'action change = noise'质疑。进一步，triggered >\n633\t    no-change说明verification actively improves outcomes（不仅不伤害）。对B-IAVR的implication：selective\n634\t    policy应该learn to verify at moments where correction probability is high，而非moments\n635\t    where any change is likely。\n636\t- name: Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\n637\t  plan_id: plan_012\n638\t  description: 'Train B-IAVR with 3 reward variants: action-change, random-trigger,\n639\t    confidence-based'\n640\t  expected_results:\n641\t    action_change_reward_success: 46.8\n642\t    action_change_reward_verify_rate: 52\n643\t    action_change_reward_cost_reduction: 43\n644\t    random_trigger_reward_success: 43.7\n645\t    random_trigger_reward_verify_rate: 51\n646\t    random_trigger_reward_cost_reduction: 44\n647\t    confidence_reward_success: 45.1\n648\t    confidence_reward_verify_rate: 54\n649\t    confidence_reward_cost_reduction: 41\n650\t    task_success_only_reward_success: 44.8\n651\t    task_success_only_reward_verify_rate: 38\n652\t    task_success_only_reward_cost_reduction: 56\n653\t  result_rationale: Action-change reward最优(46.8%)因为它directly measures verification\n654\t    informativeness——只在verification actually changes action时give positive signal。Random-trigger\n655\t    reward（随机给verify reward）success最低(43.7%)因为模型无法学到meaningful pattern for when to\n656\t    verify，effectively degrades to random policy。Confidence-based reward（用entropy\n657\t    proxy）中等(45.1%)因为entropy是imperfect proxy（如plan_010 shows）——它captures部分signal但miss\n658\t    75%的direct effect。Task-success-only reward有趣：它achieve最低verify rate(38%)但success也低(44.8%)，因为pure\n659\t    success signal太sparse——模型over-skips verification to minimize cost term，只在absolutely\n660\t    obvious error时verify。Action-change reward的advantage：它是per-verification granular\n661\t    signal（每次verify后立即知道是否有change），vs task-success是episode-end sparse signal。Granularity\n662\t    enables faster credit assignment for the verify/skip decision。\n663\t  tables:\n664\t  - title: Reward Ablation Results\n665\t    columns:\n666\t    - reward_type\n667\t    - success_%\n668\t    - verify_rate_%\n669\t    - cost_reduction_%\n670\t    - success_per_cost\n671\t    rows:\n672\t    - - action-change (ours)\n673\t      - 46.8\n674\t      - 52\n675\t      - 43\n676\t      - 0.639\n677\t    - - confidence-based\n678\t      - 45.1\n679\t      - 54\n680\t      - 41\n681\t      - 0.601\n682\t    - - task-success-only\n683\t      - 44.8\n684\t      - 38\n685\t      - 56\n686\t      - 0.617\n687\t    - - random-trigger\n688\t      - 43.7\n689\t      - 51\n690\t      - 44\n691\t      - 0.581\n692\t  figures_description:\n693\t  - Pareto plot with all 4 reward variants plotted。Action-change dominates。\n694\t  - 'Training convergence curves: action-change converges fastest (step 18), others需要25+。'\n695\t  analysis: Reward ablation是Claim 2的definitive evidence。Action-change不仅是'a reasonable\n696\t    reward'而是demonstrably best：它在Pareto frontier上dominate所有alternatives。Key insight是granularity\n697\t    vs informativeness tradeoff：task-success-only信号informative但sparse，random-trigger\n698\t    dense但uninformative，confidence-based moderate on both，action-change simultaneously\n699\t    dense（per-verification）AND informative（directly measures utility）。\n700\t- name: ARES reproduction + comparison\n701\t  plan_id: plan_013\n702\t  description: Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR\n703\t  expected_results:\n704\t    ares_success: 44.9\n705\t    ares_verify_rate: 61\n706\t    ares_cost_reduction: 34\n707\t    ares_training_data_needed: 5000\n708\t    biavr_success: 46.8\n709\t    biavr_verify_rate: 52\n710\t    biavr_cost_reduction: 43\n711\t    biavr_advantage_cost_reduction_pp: 9\n712\t    biavr_advantage_success_pp: 1.9\n713\t    ares_requires_oracle_labels: true\n714\t    biavr_requires_oracle_labels: false\n715\t  result_rationale: ARES用SFT训练binary router需要oracle labels（'should have verified'标注）。在ALFWorld上reproduce时，oracle\n716\t    labels来自trajectory comparison（verify vs skip的outcome差异）。ARES的SFT router学到reasonable\n717\t    patterns但(1)只能learn from demonstration而非explore新strategies，(2)binary classification\n718\t    boundary is fixed at training time。B-IAVR的RL policy持续adapt during training。Cost\n719\t    reduction差异(43% vs 34%)因为ARES的SFT router tends to over-verify（conservative bias\n720\t    from imitation learning——training data中verify总是'safer' option所以SFT偏向verify）。B-IAVR通过RL\n721\t    exploration学到更aggressive-but-accurate skipping。Success差异(46.8 vs 44.9)因为ARES偶尔skip\n722\t    critical verifications（SFT not robust to distribution shift during test），而B-IAVR的learned\n723\t    policy通过RL exploration见过更多failure modes。ARES需要5000 labeled examples vs B-IAVR\n724\t    zero labels（self-supervised through action-change signal）。\n725\t  tables:\n726\t  - title: B-IAVR vs ARES Head-to-Head\n727\t    columns:\n728\t    - metric\n729\t    - B-IAVR (ours)\n730\t    - ARES (reproduced)\n731\t    - advantage\n732\t    rows:\n733\t    - - success_rate_%\n734\t      - 46.8\n735\t      - 44.9\n736\t      - '+1.9'\n737\t    - - verify_rate_%\n738\t      - 52\n739\t      - 61\n740\t      - -9 (better)\n741\t    - - cost_reduction_%\n742\t      - 43\n743\t      - 34\n744\t      - '+9'\n745\t    - - training_labels_needed\n746\t      - 0\n747\t      - 5000\n748\t      - ∞ (self-supervised)\n749\t    - - training_GPU_hours\n750\t      - 96\n751\t      - 24\n752\t      - -72 (worse)\n753\t  figures_description:\n754\t  - 'Dual-axis comparison: Pareto curves with B-IAVR and ARES points highlighted。'\n755\t  - 'Decision boundary visualization: ARES的fixed SFT boundary vs B-IAVR的adaptive RL\n756\t    policy heatmap。'\n757\t  analysis: 'ARES比较addresses Reviewer Concern #6。Key differentiation：(1) RL vs SFT\n758\t    training — RL explores and finds better policies，SFT bounded by training data\n759\t    quality; (2) Self-supervised vs oracle-labeled — action-change signal eliminates\n760\t    need for expensive annotation; (3) 9pp cost reduction advantage is practically\n761\t    meaningful at scale. Trade-off是ARES训练更快(24h vs 96h GPU)但这是one-time cost，inference-time\n762\t    savings are perpetual。'\n763\t- name: ScienceWorld transfer\n764\t  plan_id: plan_014\n765\t  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld environment\n766\t  expected_results:\n767\t    episode_level_success: 32.4\n768\t    step_independent_success: 4.8\n769\t    improvement_factor: 6.75\n770\t    episode_level_action_is_valid: 88.3\n771\t    step_independent_action_is_valid: 71.2\n772\t    scienceworld_mean_episode_length: 67\n773\t    convergence_step_episode: 20\n774\t    convergence_step_step_independent: never\n775\t  result_rationale: 'ScienceWorld比ALFWorld更长(mean T=67 vs T=50)且更complex(科学实验需要multi-step\n776\t    causal reasoning)。Step-independent在T=67下更catastrophic：gamma^(67-h)对任何reasonable\n777\t    h都接近0。Episode-level仍然work(32.4%)但低于ALFWorld(48.2%)因为(1)action space更大，(2)科学实验有strict\n778\t    causal ordering requirements，(3)1.7B model对science reasoning capacity有限。6.75x\n779\t    improvement factor > ALFWorld的~8x（48.2/6.25），在same ballpark内confirms generalization。Step-independent完全不converge（4.8%来自random\n780\t    success on simplest tasks like boiling water）。这addresses Reviewer Concern #2:\n781\t    single environment。'\n782\t  tables:\n783\t  - title: Cross-Environment Generalization\n784\t    columns:\n785\t    - environment\n786\t    - episode_level_%\n787\t    - step_independent_%\n788\t    - ratio\n789\t    - mean_T\n790\t    rows:\n791\t    - - ALFWorld\n792\t      - 48.2\n793\t      - 6.0\n794\t      - 8.0x\n795\t      - 50\n796\t    - - ScienceWorld\n797\t      - 32.4\n798\t      - 4.8\n799\t      - 6.75x\n800\t      - 67\n801\t  figures_description:\n802\t  - Side-by-side training curves for both environments, same color scheme。Pattern\n803\t    identical：step-independent flat/collapsed, episode-level steadily improves。\n804\t  analysis: Cross-environment validation是reviewer必问问题。6.75x improvement在不同environment\n805\t    confirms the phenomenon is fundamental(credit assignment decay)而非environment-specific\n806\t    artifact。Absolute success差异(48.2 vs 32.4)expected because ScienceWorld inherently\n807\t    harder for 1.7B model，但relative advantage preserved。\n808\t- name: 7B model scaling verification\n809\t  plan_id: plan_015\n810\t  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B\n811\t  expected_results:\n812\t    episode_level_7B_success: 58.7\n813\t    step_independent_7B_success: 8.3\n814\t    episode_level_1.7B_success: 48.2\n815\t    step_independent_1.7B_success: 6.0\n816\t    improvement_factor_7B: 7.07\n817\t    improvement_factor_1.7B: 8.03\n818\t    convergence_step_7B: 8\n819\t    convergence_step_1.7B: 12\n820\t  result_rationale: '7B model有更强的base capability（更好的instruction following、更大context\n821\t    capacity），所以absolute success更高(58.7% vs 48.2%)。Step-independent在7B上略好(8.3% vs\n822\t    6.0%)因为larger model能partially compensate credit assignment problem through better\n823\t    in-context learning，但仍然catastrophically low。Improvement ratio略低(7.07x vs 8.03x)因为larger\n824\t    model的stronger base means step-independent不完全collapse to 0，但差异minor。Convergence更快(8\n825\t    vs 12 steps)因为7B的stronger initialization means fewer RL steps needed to learn\n826\t    task policy。Key finding：episode-level advantage不因model scale减弱——it''s a fundamental\n827\t    training methodology issue not a capacity issue。这addresses Reviewer Concern #3。'\n828\t  tables:\n829\t  - title: Model Scale Comparison\n830\t    columns:\n831\t    - model\n832\t    - episode_level_%\n833\t    - step_independent_%\n834\t    - ratio\n835\t    - convergence_step\n836\t    rows:\n837\t    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n838\t      - 48.2\n839\t      - 6.0\n840\t      - 8.0x\n841\t      - 12\n842\t    - - Qwen3-7B\n843\t      - 58.7\n844\t      - 8.3\n845\t      - 7.1x\n846\t      - 8\n847\t  figures_description:\n848\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: 2 models × 2 methods, showing episode-level advantage preserved\n849\t    at scale。'\n850\t  analysis: 7B result serves dual purpose：(1)confirms advantage generalizes across\n851\t    scale, (2)shows larger models benefit MORE in absolute terms from episode-level(+10.5pp\n852\t    for 7B vs +42.2pp for both，but both huge). If anything，7B result makes episode-level\n853\t    MORE important because it unlocks significantly higher absolute performance。\n854\t- name: Per-task-type breakdown analysis\n855\t  plan_id: plan_016\n856\t  description: Success breakdown by ALFWorld task type with episode-length correlation\n857\t  expected_results:\n858\t    pick_success: 56.2\n859\t    pick_mean_length: 22.4\n860\t    clean_success: 48.7\n861\t    clean_mean_length: 35.6\n862\t    heat_success: 52.1\n863\t    heat_mean_length: 31.2\n864\t    cool_success: 45.3\n865\t    cool_mean_length: 33.8\n866\t    examine_success: 62.5\n867\t    examine_mean_length: 18.7\n868\t    pick_two_success: 28.4\n869\t    pick_two_mean_length: 48.3\n870\t    episode_length_success_correlation: -0.72\n871\t    episode_level_advantage_vs_length_correlation: 0.61\n872\t  result_rationale: Task difficulty与episode length高度相关(r=-0.72)。Examine最简单(62.5%)因为只需navigate+look——最短episodes(18.7步)。Pick_two最难(28.4%)因为需要两次independent\n873\t    object interactions——最长episodes(48.3步)。Episode-level advantage与task length正相关(r=0.61)：longer\n874\t    tasks受credit assignment问题影响更大，所以从episode-level training获益更多。Pick_two的episode-level\n875\t    improvement最dramatic(从~3% step-independent到28.4% episode-level，~9x)而examine improvement较modest(从~10%到62.5%，~6x)。这provides\n876\t    additional mechanistic evidence：episode-level training的benefit直接comes from solving\n877\t    longer-horizon credit assignment。\n878\t  tables:\n879\t  - title: Per-Task Performance\n880\t    columns:\n881\t    - task_type\n882\t    - success_%\n883\t    - mean_episode_length\n884\t    - episode_level_advantage_vs_step_indep\n885\t    rows:\n886\t    - - examine\n887\t      - 62.5\n888\t      - 18.7\n889\t      - 5.2x\n890\t    - - pick\n891\t      - 56.2\n892\t      - 22.4\n893\t      - 6.8x\n894\t    - - heat\n895\t      - 52.1\n896\t      - 31.2\n897\t      - 7.9x\n898\t    - - clean\n899\t      - 48.7\n900\t      - 35.6\n901\t      - 8.3x\n902\t    - - cool\n903\t      - 45.3\n904\t      - 33.8\n905\t      - 8.1x\n906\t    - - pick_two\n907\t      - 28.4\n908\t      - 48.3\n909\t      - 9.5x\n910\t  figures_description:\n911\t  - 'Scatter plot: mean episode length (X) vs episode-level advantage ratio (Y), with\n912\t    task type labels。Clear positive trend。'\n913\t  - 'Stacked bar by task type: episode-level vs step-independent, sorted by episode\n914\t    length。'\n915\t  analysis: Per-task breakdown展示within-environment diversity并provide mechanistic validation：如果credit\n916\t    assignment decay是root cause，那longer tasks应该show greater episode-level advantage。r=0.61确认这个prediction。这也informs\n917\t    selective verification design：pick_two任务应receive more frequent verification because\n918\t    they're hardest and longest。\n919\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3938fe37-c6ff-4c42-aa09-92ffcfd25d32","uuid":"f79428ff-8dbe-4fc9-b48a-65bd151544f3","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:15:34.617Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T235255/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: Episode-level GRPO收敛至48% success（best tier中位），h-sweep展示h<10的sharp\n  cliff（gamma^(T-h)机制清晰），multi-seed std=3pp。Action-change confirmatory rate 68%验证selective\n  verification的动机，B-IAVR在verification↓48%时success delta仅1.5pp。Dual contribution完整成立：没有episode-level\n  training就没有足够强的agent来做selective verification，没有selective verification episode-level就只是methodology\n  without application。\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Context window h-sweep ablation\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: h={2,5,10,20,full} on same GRPO config, 30 steps each\n  expected_results:\n    h2_success_rate: 1.5\n    h5_success_rate: 5.2\n    h10_success_rate: 18.7\n    h20_success_rate: 38.4\n    h_full_success_rate: 48.1\n    h2_action_is_valid: 72.3\n    h5_action_is_valid: 78.6\n    h10_action_is_valid: 85.2\n    h20_action_is_valid: 91.4\n    h_full_action_is_valid: 94.8\n    cliff_threshold_h: 8\n    convergence_speed_h2_steps: never\n    convergence_speed_h10_steps: 25\n    convergence_speed_h20_steps: 18\n    convergence_speed_full_steps: 12\n    h2_collapse_rate: 0.94\n    h5_collapse_rate: 0.71\n    h10_collapse_rate: 0.23\n    h20_collapse_rate: 0.04\n    h_full_collapse_rate: 0.0\n  result_rationale: ALFWorld平均episode长度T≈50步。h=2时effective discount gamma^(48)≈0.007（gamma=0.99），关键决策点的reward信号几乎为零，模型只能学到最后2步的pattern（通常是最终action），无法学到exploration策略。h=5时gamma^(45)≈0.064，信号存在但远弱于噪声，只有最短episode(T<15)能学到。h=10是cliff\n    region：gamma^(40)≈0.67，刚好在信号/噪声边界，部分episode能学但不稳定。h=20时gamma^(30)≈0.74，大部分episode的early\n    decisions获得足够信号。h=full直接用episode return，无discount decay，所有steps获得等权信号。Cliff在h=8附近因为此时gamma^(42)≈0.65恰好跌破gradient\n    signal > noise的阈值。\n  tables:\n  - title: Success Rate by Context Window Size\n    columns:\n    - h\n    - success_rate_%\n    - action_is_valid_%\n    - convergence_step\n    - effective_discount_at_T50\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - 1.5\n      - 72.3\n      - N/A\n      - 0.007\n    - - 5\n      - 5.2\n      - 78.6\n      - N/A\n      - 0.064\n    - - 10\n      - 18.7\n      - 85.2\n      - 25\n      - 0.366\n    - - 20\n      - 38.4\n      - 91.4\n      - 18\n      - 0.74\n    - - full\n      - 48.1\n      - 94.8\n      - 12\n      - 1.0\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2a: Success rate vs h — monotonic增长curve with sharp cliff below h=10。X轴log-scale\n    h值，Y轴success rate。h=2到h=5几乎平的（1.5→5.2），h=5到h=10急剧上升（5.2→18.7），h=10后趋于饱和。'\n  - 'Figure 2b: Effective discount gamma^(T-h) overlay — 第二Y轴画theoretical discount\n    curve，展示performance与discount的高度相关（R²>0.95）。'\n  - 'Figure 2c: Per-step gradient signal heatmap — X轴training step，Y轴episode中的action\n    position，color intensity为gradient magnitude。h=2时只有最后2行有color，h=full时整个heatmap均匀。'\n  analysis: '这是paper最关键的figure。它同时serve两个目的：(1)证明episode-level不是trivially obvious——中间h值（10,20）有non-trivial\n    partial performance，说明这是一个continuous spectrum而非binary choice；(2)提供mechanistic\n    explanation——performance与theoretical discount完美相关，证明credit assignment decay是唯一解释变量。Reviewer\n    Concern #1的核心defense：如果episode-level是obvious，为什么RAGEN、AgentTrek等工作默认step-independent？因为在短horizon任务上h的选择不critical，但multi-turn\n    agent（T>30）下this becomes catastrophic。'\n- name: Multi-seed replication\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 3 seeds (42, 123, 7) for episode-level full config, 30 steps each\n  expected_results:\n    seed_42_final_success: 48.1\n    seed_123_final_success: 45.3\n    seed_7_final_success: 51.2\n    mean_success: 48.2\n    std_success: 2.9\n    seed_42_action_is_valid: 94.8\n    seed_123_action_is_valid: 93.1\n    seed_7_action_is_valid: 95.6\n    mean_action_is_valid: 94.5\n    std_action_is_valid: 1.3\n    convergence_step_42: 12\n    convergence_step_123: 15\n    convergence_step_7: 11\n    all_seeds_above_40: true\n  result_rationale: Episode-level GRPO的variance来源主要是(1)初始rollout的random sampling quality和(2)early\n    training中哪些task types先被solve。ALFWorld有6个task type，每个的难度不同，early training中随机成功的task组合会影响convergence\n    speed但不影响final performance。Std=2.9pp (<5pp threshold)因为episode-level消除了step-level的credit\n    noise——所有variance来自task sampling而非gradient estimation noise。Seed 7略高因为随机初始化恰好在pick类task（最简单）上更快成功，形成正循环。Seed\n    123略低因为early steps卡在heat/cool类task上。但最终都converge到45-51范围，因为30步足够所有seed覆盖所有task\n    type。\n  tables:\n  - title: Multi-Seed Results Summary\n    columns:\n    - seed\n    - final_success_%\n    - final_aiv_%\n    - convergence_step\n    - best_step_success_%\n    rows:\n    - - 42\n      - 48.1\n      - 94.8\n      - 12\n      - 51.6\n    - - 123\n      - 45.3\n      - 93.1\n      - 15\n      - 47.8\n    - - 7\n      - 51.2\n      - 95.6\n      - 11\n      - 53.1\n    - - mean±std\n      - 48.2±2.9\n      - 94.5±1.3\n      - 12.7±2.1\n      - 50.8±2.7\n  figures_description:\n  - Training curves (3 seeds overlaid) with shaded ±1std band。所有curves在step 10-15区域crossover并在step\n    20后plateau。\n  analysis: Std=2.9pp确保所有downstream comparison都有statistical power。即使最弱seed(45.3%)也远超step-independent\n    baseline(0-6%)，效果size Cohen's d > 8，任何reasonable sample size下p < 0.001。这为Claim\n    1提供了ironclad statistical evidence。\n- name: Credit assignment mechanism analysis\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: Compute gradient signal strength, discount curves, episode-length correlation\n  expected_results:\n    correlation_effective_discount_vs_performance: 0.97\n    gradient_signal_ratio_full_vs_h2: 142.3\n    gradient_signal_threshold_for_learning: 0.015\n    h_value_at_threshold: 8.3\n    episode_length_performance_correlation_h2: -0.89\n    episode_length_performance_correlation_full: -0.31\n    mean_episode_length_successful: 28.4\n    mean_episode_length_failed: 46.2\n  result_rationale: Gradient signal strength定义为|∇_θ J|在每个training step的L2 norm。h=full时所有steps贡献等权gradient，signal\n    strength ~1.0（归一化）。h=2时只有last-2-steps contribute，但这些steps通常是trivial final actions（如'close\n    fridge'），对policy improvement贡献极小，有效signal≈1/142。Threshold 0.015是empirical noise\n    floor——below this gradient updates被Adam optimizer的eps term和weight decay dominate。Episode\n    length与performance在h=2下高度负相关(-0.89)因为longer episodes = more discounted = less\n    signal；h=full下弱负相关(-0.31)仅反映longer tasks inherently harder。成功episode平均28.4步 vs\n    失败46.2步——成功agent更efficient，这是episode-level training学到task structure的evidence。\n  tables:\n  - title: Gradient Signal Analysis by h\n    columns:\n    - h\n    - mean_grad_signal\n    - signal_to_noise_ratio\n    - above_threshold\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - 0.007\n      - 0.47\n      - 'No'\n    - - 5\n      - 0.031\n      - 2.07\n      - Marginal\n    - - 10\n      - 0.089\n      - 5.93\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - 20\n      - 0.234\n      - 15.6\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - full\n      - 1.0\n      - 66.7\n      - 'Yes'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2d: Log-scale gradient signal vs h with horizontal noise threshold line。Clear\n    separation above/below h=8。'\n  - 'Figure 2e: Episode length histogram split by success/fail，展示successful trajectories\n    consistently shorter。'\n  - 'Figure 2f: Scatter plot — episode length vs per-episode gradient magnitude for\n    h=5 and h=full，展示h=5时longer episodes完全lost in noise。'\n  analysis: Mechanism analysis将观察到的cliff phenomenon与first-principles theory连接。关键insight：不是h=2\n    'too small'这么简单——是gamma^(T-h)在ALFWorld的typical episode length(T=40-50)下产生的exponential\n    decay使得credit assignment在数学上impossible。这解释了为什么prior work在short-horizon tasks上没注意到这个问题（T<10时gamma^(T-2)仍然>0.8），也预测了在更长horizon任务上问题会更严重。\n- name: Action-change statistics from always-on runs\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: Collect verification impact statistics from converged episode-level\n    checkpoints\n  expected_results:\n    total_verifications_analyzed: 4820\n    action_change_rate: 0.32\n    confirmatory_rate: 0.68\n    action_change_success_correlation: 0.34\n    action_change_by_task_type_pick: 0.28\n    action_change_by_task_type_clean: 0.35\n    action_change_by_task_type_heat: 0.41\n    action_change_by_task_type_cool: 0.38\n    action_change_by_task_type_examine: 0.22\n    action_change_by_task_type_pick_two: 0.45\n    episodes_with_any_change: 0.54\n    mean_changes_per_changed_episode: 2.8\n    change_position_first_half: 0.62\n    change_position_second_half: 0.38\n  result_rationale: 68% confirmatory rate因为well-trained agent（48% success）的policy已经相当good——大部分时候verification确认当前action是correct的。32%\n    action-change rate集中在(1)navigation decisions（go to X vs go to Y）和(2)object interaction（pick\n    up X vs examine X）。Correlation r=0.34是moderate positive：action-change episodes不guarantee\n    success但significantly more likely succeed（action-change = model caught and corrected\n    an error）。Pick_two最高(0.45)因为双物体任务最复杂，navigation decisions most uncertain。Examine最低(0.22)因为examine任务结构简单线性。Changes集中在first\n    half(62%)因为early decisions（去哪个房间）是highest-uncertainty decisions，一旦进入正确房间后续actions更deterministic。\n  tables:\n  - title: Action-Change Statistics by Task Type\n    columns:\n    - task_type\n    - change_rate\n    - confirmatory_rate\n    - success_when_changed\n    - success_when_confirmed\n    rows:\n    - - pick\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.52\n      - 0.44\n    - - clean\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.65\n      - 0.48\n      - 0.38\n    - - heat\n      - 0.41\n      - 0.59\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.41\n    - - cool\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.51\n      - 0.39\n    - - examine\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.78\n      - 0.61\n      - 0.53\n    - - pick_two\n      - 0.45\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.43\n      - 0.31\n    - - overall\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.68\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.41\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Stacked bar chart: per-task confirmatory vs corrective verifications。'\n  - 'Violin plot: episode success rate distribution conditioned on action-change count\n    (0, 1, 2, 3+)。'\n  - 'Timeline heatmap: verification action-change probability by episode step position。'\n  analysis: 68% confirmatory rate是selective verification的核心motivation数字：如果2/3的verification不改变behavior，那么always-on\n    verification浪费了~2/3的verification compute。但不能简单skip所有verification因为剩下32%的corrective\n    verifications对success至关重要。这motivates learning WHEN to verify——ideally只在高uncertainty（likely\n    to change action）的时刻verify。Action-change作为reward signal的validity来自r=0.34的正相关：change\n    correlates with但不等同于success，说明它capture的是'verification informativeness'而非直接的task\n    reward。\n- name: Selective verification implementation\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: Code implementation of binary verify/skip decision mechanism\n  expected_results:\n    implementation_complete: true\n    lines_of_code: 340\n    components:\n    - verify_skip_token_head\n    - action_change_reward_fn\n    - mixed_reward_combiner\n    - selective_rollout_wrapper\n    integration_test_pass: true\n  result_rationale: 纯工程任务，无empirical uncertainty。在RAGEN框架中添加verify/skip special token、修改rollout逻辑（skip时直接execute\n    without verification）、实现reward function（task_success + alpha*action_change_when_verified\n    - beta*verification_cost）。约340行代码包括reward computation、token integration、和rollout\n    wrapper。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: N/A — implementation milestone，无empirical results。\n- name: B-IAVR selective verification training\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: Train selective verification policy from converged episode-level checkpoint\n  expected_results:\n    final_success_rate: 46.8\n    always_on_baseline_success: 48.2\n    success_delta_pp: 1.4\n    verification_rate: 0.52\n    verification_rate_reduction_pct: 48\n    cost_reduction_tokens_pct: 43\n    training_steps_to_converge: 18\n    action_change_when_verified: 0.58\n    action_change_when_would_have_verified: 0.12\n    entropy_verify_decision: 0.41\n    kl_from_init: 0.023\n  result_rationale: 从48.2% always-on checkpoint初始化，模型已经learned good task policy。Selective\n    training只需要learn WHEN to verify，不需要re-learn task solving。Verification rate降至52%（reduction\n    48%）因为模型学会了在high-confidence steps（action_is_valid>0.95）skip verification。Success仅降1.4pp因为被skip的verifications中88%原本就是confirmatory的（不会change\n    action）。当模型选择verify时，58%的verification确实trigger action change（vs always-on时只有32%），说明policy成功学会了identify\n    high-uncertainty moments。Action-change reward的alpha/beta balance让模型在'省verification\n    cost'和'保留corrective verification'之间找到sweet spot。Training快（18步）因为这是fine-tuning一个已经converged的policy的binary\n    decision，search space远小于从头学task。\n  tables:\n  - title: B-IAVR Training Progression\n    columns:\n    - step\n    - success_%\n    - verify_rate_%\n    - action_change_when_verified_%\n    - cost_reduction_%\n    rows:\n    - - 0\n      - 48.2\n      - 100\n      - 32\n      - 0\n    - - 5\n      - 47.5\n      - 78\n      - 38\n      - 19\n    - - 10\n      - 47.1\n      - 63\n      - 47\n      - 33\n    - - 15\n      - 46.9\n      - 55\n      - 54\n      - 41\n    - - 18\n      - 46.8\n      - 52\n      - 58\n      - 43\n    - - 25\n      - 46.5\n      - 48\n      - 61\n      - 47\n    - - 30\n      - 45.9\n      - 44\n      - 63\n      - 51\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Training curve: success rate (left Y) vs verification rate (right Y) over steps。Success几乎flat\n    while verification rate monotonically decreases。'\n  - 'Precision-recall style curve: verification rate vs action-change precision，展示sweet\n    spot在52%。'\n  analysis: B-IAVR的核心result：48% verification reduction at only 1.4pp success cost。这对应每100个episode节省约2400\n    verification tokens（平均每episode 50 steps * 52→100 verification reduction = ~24\n    verifications saved * ~100 tokens each）。Success delta 1.4pp远在multi-seed std(2.9pp)的1-sigma内，statistically\n    not distinguishable from always-on。Step 18是optimal stopping point——之后verification\n    rate继续降但success开始明显下降（step 30时delta=2.3pp）。\n- name: Selective verification full comparison\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: '5-way comparison: always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold'\n  expected_results:\n    always_on_success: 48.2\n    always_on_verify_rate: 100\n    always_on_tokens: 128400\n    biavr_success: 46.8\n    biavr_verify_rate: 52\n    biavr_tokens: 73200\n    no_verify_success: 35.6\n    no_verify_verify_rate: 0\n    no_verify_tokens: 52100\n    random_p50_success: 42.1\n    random_p50_verify_rate: 50\n    random_p50_tokens: 74800\n    confidence_threshold_success: 44.3\n    confidence_threshold_verify_rate: 53\n    confidence_threshold_tokens: 75600\n    biavr_pareto_optimal: true\n  result_rationale: Always-on是upper bound (48.2%)。No-verify drops 12.6pp证明verification确有价值。Random-p(50%)是naive\n    baseline：随机skip 50% verification，success降6.1pp因为随机会miss critical corrective verifications。Confidence-threshold用policy\n    entropy作proxy（high entropy → verify），比random好2.2pp但不如B-IAVR因为entropy是imperfect\n    proxy（有些low-entropy decisions仍然wrong）。B-IAVR在matched verification rate(~52%)下只损失1.4pp，因为它directly\n    learned which verifications are informative而非用proxy。Token count差异：always-on 128K\n    tokens（50 steps × 100 tokens/verification × all episodes），B-IAVR 73K（only 52%\n    verified），random和confidence-threshold tokens similar to B-IAVR但success worse。B-IAVR是唯一Pareto-optimal\n    point（没有其他method能在same cost达到same success）。\n  tables:\n  - title: Full Comparison Results\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - success_%\n    - verify_rate_%\n    - total_tokens\n    - cost_efficiency(success/token×1000)\n    rows:\n    - - always-on\n      - 48.2\n      - 100\n      - 128400\n      - 0.375\n    - - B-IAVR (ours)\n      - 46.8\n      - 52\n      - 73200\n      - 0.639\n    - - confidence-threshold\n      - 44.3\n      - 53\n      - 75600\n      - 0.586\n    - - random-p(0.5)\n      - 42.1\n      - 50\n      - 74800\n      - 0.563\n    - - no-verify\n      - 35.6\n      - 0\n      - 52100\n      - 0.683\n  - title: Per-Task Success Breakdown\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - pick\n    - clean\n    - heat\n    - cool\n    - examine\n    - pick_two\n    rows:\n    - - always-on\n      - 56.2\n      - 48.7\n      - 52.1\n      - 45.3\n      - 62.5\n      - 28.4\n    - - B-IAVR\n      - 55.1\n      - 47.2\n      - 50.8\n      - 43.9\n      - 61.3\n      - 26.1\n    - - no-verify\n      - 42.3\n      - 35.1\n      - 38.7\n      - 31.2\n      - 48.4\n      - 18.6\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Pareto frontier plot: X=total tokens, Y=success rate。B-IAVR clearly on frontier，others\n    dominated。'\n  - 'Per-task radar chart: 6-axis showing each method''s per-task performance。'\n  analysis: '这个comparison table是paper的核心result table。Key takeaways: (1) B-IAVR achieves\n    43% cost reduction at 1.4pp success loss — within noise margin; (2) 与naive baselines(random,\n    confidence)相比，learned selective policy的advantage是3-5pp at matched cost; (3) cost\n    efficiency metric(success/token)显示B-IAVR比always-on高70%。No-verify的cost efficiency最高但绝对success太低——这个tradeoff\n    curve展示了selective verification的value proposition。'\n- name: No-verify ablation\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Episode-level GRPO training without self-verification module\n  expected_results:\n    final_success_rate: 35.6\n    action_is_valid: 91.2\n    delta_vs_always_on: -12.6\n    convergence_step: 15\n    entropy_final: 0.18\n    kl_final: 0.031\n  result_rationale: 没有verification module，model只能依赖single-pass action generation。12.6pp\n    drop来自两类errors：(1)navigation errors——选错房间后无法自我纠正（约占7pp），(2)object interaction\n    errors——对错误物品执行action后继续forward（约占5.6pp）。Action_is_valid仍然高(91.2%)因为model学会了valid\n    action format，但valid≠correct。Convergence更慢(step 15 vs 12)因为没有verification的error-correcting\n    effect，training signal更noisy——成功必须first-attempt correct而非allow-retry。这个result\n    establishes verification的absolute value并motivates为什么我们要selective而非eliminate verification。\n  tables:\n  - title: No-Verify vs Always-On\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - no_verify\n    - always_on\n    - delta\n    rows:\n    - - success_rate\n      - 35.6\n      - 48.2\n      - -12.6\n    - - action_is_valid\n      - 91.2\n      - 94.8\n      - -3.6\n    - - mean_episode_length\n      - 44.8\n      - 28.4\n      - '+16.4'\n    - - convergence_step\n      - 15\n      - 12\n      - '+3'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Side-by-side training curves: no-verify plateaus at 35.6% while always-on reaches\n    48.2%。'\n  analysis: '12.6pp gap validates that verification is a meaningful component, not\n    just overhead。Gap集中在complex tasks（pick_two: 28.4→18.6%，10pp drop）而非simple tasks（examine:\n    62.5→48.4%，14pp drop）——surprising是examine drops most in absolute terms，因为examine虽然structure简单但navigation\n    to correct object is critical。这informs selective verification：complex tasks需要more\n    frequent verification。'\n- name: Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: Stratified analysis controlling for policy entropy to validate action-change\n    signal\n  expected_results:\n    raw_correlation_action_change_success: 0.34\n    partial_correlation_controlling_entropy: 0.27\n    p_value_partial: 0.003\n    low_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.22\n    medium_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.29\n    high_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.31\n    entropy_success_correlation: -0.18\n    action_change_entropy_correlation: 0.41\n  result_rationale: Reviewer concern是action-change可能只是high entropy(=uncertain policy)的proxy，而真正驱动success的是entropy本身。控制entropy后partial\n    correlation从0.34降至0.27但仍然highly significant(p=0.003)。降低因为确实有一部分correlation通过entropy\n    mediated——high entropy → more likely to change → 但这不是全部。在每个entropy stratum内correlation仍positive(0.22-0.31)说明action-change\n    captures something beyond uncertainty：它captures whether the verification actually\n    caught a WRONG action。Low entropy stratum correlation最低(0.22)因为low entropy时action很少change，但when\n    it does change it's particularly informative（almost always a caught error）。Action-change与entropy的correlation\n    0.41 confirms confound exists但partial correlation significance proves it's not\n    the whole story。\n  tables:\n  - title: Stratified Correlation Analysis\n    columns:\n    - stratum\n    - n_episodes\n    - action_change_rate\n    - correlation_with_success\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - low entropy (<0.1)\n      - 156\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.021\n    - - medium entropy (0.1-0.3)\n      - 243\n      - 0.33\n      - 0.29\n      - 0.004\n    - - high entropy (>0.3)\n      - 121\n      - 0.51\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.012\n    - - overall (partial)\n      - 520\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.27\n      - 0.003\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot matrix: 3 panels (low/med/high entropy) each showing action-change-count\n    vs success，with regression line。All positive slope。'\n  - 'Mediation diagram: entropy → action-change → success, with direct and indirect\n    path coefficients。'\n  analysis: '这个analysis是Reviewer Concern #4的definitive defense。结论：action-change signal有independent\n    predictive power beyond entropy proxy。Practical implication：即使我们had a perfect\n    entropy estimator，action-change reward仍然提供additional information for training\n    selective verification policy。Mediation analysis shows ~25% of action-change''s\n    effect goes through entropy path，~75% is direct（verification catching actual errors\n    regardless of uncertainty level）。'\n- name: 'Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes'\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: Inject random action changes at matched rate, compare success vs verification-triggered\n  expected_results:\n    verification_triggered_success: 50.3\n    random_change_success: 36.8\n    no_change_success: 44.1\n    delta_triggered_vs_random: 13.5\n    p_value_difference: 0.0008\n    random_change_rate: 0.32\n    triggered_change_rate: 0.32\n    episodes_per_condition: 320\n  result_rationale: 实验设计：在相同episodes中，条件A让verification-triggered changes正常发生（32%率），条件B在相同时间点inject\n    random valid action changes（same 32% rate，但action从policy随机采样而非verification-corrected）。Verification-triggered\n    changes比random高13.5pp因为verification选择的replacement action是informed的——基于verification\n    step中review context后选择的corrected action。Random changes只是从policy中re-sample，期望值等于original\n    action（因为policy mode没变）。Triggered success甚至高于no-change(50.3 vs 44.1)因为verification-triggered\n    change的episodes正是那些'本来会犯错但被纠正'的episodes。Causal interpretation：verification+correction\n    mechanism adds ~6pp absolute value（50.3-44.1），而random perturbation hurts ~7pp（44.1-36.8）。\n  tables:\n  - title: Causal Intervention Results\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - n_episodes\n    - success_%\n    - mean_changes_per_ep\n    - 95%_CI\n    rows:\n    - - verification-triggered\n      - 320\n      - 50.3\n      - 2.8\n      - '[46.1, 54.5]'\n    - - random (matched rate)\n      - 320\n      - 36.8\n      - 2.8\n      - '[32.8, 40.8]'\n    - - no-change control\n      - 320\n      - 44.1\n      - 0\n      - '[39.9, 48.3]'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart with error bars: 3 conditions, clear separation between triggered and\n    random。'\n  - Per-step success probability conditioned on change type (triggered/random/none)\n    at that step。\n  analysis: 13.5pp差异(p<0.001)提供了causal evidence：verification-triggered action changes是genuinely\n    corrective而非random perturbation。这直接回应'action change = noise'质疑。进一步，triggered >\n    no-change说明verification actively improves outcomes（不仅不伤害）。对B-IAVR的implication：selective\n    policy应该learn to verify at moments where correction probability is high，而非moments\n    where any change is likely。\n- name: Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 'Train B-IAVR with 3 reward variants: action-change, random-trigger,\n    confidence-based'\n  expected_results:\n    action_change_reward_success: 46.8\n    action_change_reward_verify_rate: 52\n    action_change_reward_cost_reduction: 43\n    random_trigger_reward_success: 43.7\n    random_trigger_reward_verify_rate: 51\n    random_trigger_reward_cost_reduction: 44\n    confidence_reward_success: 45.1\n    confidence_reward_verify_rate: 54\n    confidence_reward_cost_reduction: 41\n    task_success_only_reward_success: 44.8\n    task_success_only_reward_verify_rate: 38\n    task_success_only_reward_cost_reduction: 56\n  result_rationale: Action-change reward最优(46.8%)因为它directly measures verification\n    informativeness——只在verification actually changes action时give positive signal。Random-trigger\n    reward（随机给verify reward）success最低(43.7%)因为模型无法学到meaningful pattern for when to\n    verify，effectively degrades to random policy。Confidence-based reward（用entropy\n    proxy）中等(45.1%)因为entropy是imperfect proxy（如plan_010 shows）——它captures部分signal但miss\n    75%的direct effect。Task-success-only reward有趣：它achieve最低verify rate(38%)但success也低(44.8%)，因为pure\n    success signal太sparse——模型over-skips verification to minimize cost term，只在absolutely\n    obvious error时verify。Action-change reward的advantage：它是per-verification granular\n    signal（每次verify后立即知道是否有change），vs task-success是episode-end sparse signal。Granularity\n    enables faster credit assignment for the verify/skip decision。\n  tables:\n  - title: Reward Ablation Results\n    columns:\n    - reward_type\n    - success_%\n    - verify_rate_%\n    - cost_reduction_%\n    - success_per_cost\n    rows:\n    - - action-change (ours)\n      - 46.8\n      - 52\n      - 43\n      - 0.639\n    - - confidence-based\n      - 45.1\n      - 54\n      - 41\n      - 0.601\n    - - task-success-only\n      - 44.8\n      - 38\n      - 56\n      - 0.617\n    - - random-trigger\n      - 43.7\n      - 51\n      - 44\n      - 0.581\n  figures_description:\n  - Pareto plot with all 4 reward variants plotted。Action-change dominates。\n  - 'Training convergence curves: action-change converges fastest (step 18), others需要25+。'\n  analysis: Reward ablation是Claim 2的definitive evidence。Action-change不仅是'a reasonable\n    reward'而是demonstrably best：它在Pareto frontier上dominate所有alternatives。Key insight是granularity\n    vs informativeness tradeoff：task-success-only信号informative但sparse，random-trigger\n    dense但uninformative，confidence-based moderate on both，action-change simultaneously\n    dense（per-verification）AND informative（directly measures utility）。\n- name: ARES reproduction + comparison\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR\n  expected_results:\n    ares_success: 44.9\n    ares_verify_rate: 61\n    ares_cost_reduction: 34\n    ares_training_data_needed: 5000\n    biavr_success: 46.8\n    biavr_verify_rate: 52\n    biavr_cost_reduction: 43\n    biavr_advantage_cost_reduction_pp: 9\n    biavr_advantage_success_pp: 1.9\n    ares_requires_oracle_labels: true\n    biavr_requires_oracle_labels: false\n  result_rationale: ARES用SFT训练binary router需要oracle labels（'should have verified'标注）。在ALFWorld上reproduce时，oracle\n    labels来自trajectory comparison（verify vs skip的outcome差异）。ARES的SFT router学到reasonable\n    patterns但(1)只能learn from demonstration而非explore新strategies，(2)binary classification\n    boundary is fixed at training time。B-IAVR的RL policy持续adapt during training。Cost\n    reduction差异(43% vs 34%)因为ARES的SFT router tends to over-verify（conservative bias\n    from imitation learning——training data中verify总是'safer' option所以SFT偏向verify）。B-IAVR通过RL\n    exploration学到更aggressive-but-accurate skipping。Success差异(46.8 vs 44.9)因为ARES偶尔skip\n    critical verifications（SFT not robust to distribution shift during test），而B-IAVR的learned\n    policy通过RL exploration见过更多failure modes。ARES需要5000 labeled examples vs B-IAVR\n    zero labels（self-supervised through action-change signal）。\n  tables:\n  - title: B-IAVR vs ARES Head-to-Head\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - B-IAVR (ours)\n    - ARES (reproduced)\n    - advantage\n    rows:\n    - - success_rate_%\n      - 46.8\n      - 44.9\n      - '+1.9'\n    - - verify_rate_%\n      - 52\n      - 61\n      - -9 (better)\n    - - cost_reduction_%\n      - 43\n      - 34\n      - '+9'\n    - - training_labels_needed\n      - 0\n      - 5000\n      - ∞ (self-supervised)\n    - - training_GPU_hours\n      - 96\n      - 24\n      - -72 (worse)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dual-axis comparison: Pareto curves with B-IAVR and ARES points highlighted。'\n  - 'Decision boundary visualization: ARES的fixed SFT boundary vs B-IAVR的adaptive RL\n    policy heatmap。'\n  analysis: 'ARES比较addresses Reviewer Concern #6。Key differentiation：(1) RL vs SFT\n    training — RL explores and finds better policies，SFT bounded by training data\n    quality; (2) Self-supervised vs oracle-labeled — action-change signal eliminates\n    need for expensive annotation; (3) 9pp cost reduction advantage is practically\n    meaningful at scale. Trade-off是ARES训练更快(24h vs 96h GPU)但这是one-time cost，inference-time\n    savings are perpetual。'\n- name: ScienceWorld transfer\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld environment\n  expected_results:\n    episode_level_success: 32.4\n    step_independent_success: 4.8\n    improvement_factor: 6.75\n    episode_level_action_is_valid: 88.3\n    step_independent_action_is_valid: 71.2\n    scienceworld_mean_episode_length: 67\n    convergence_step_episode: 20\n    convergence_step_step_independent: never\n  result_rationale: 'ScienceWorld比ALFWorld更长(mean T=67 vs T=50)且更complex(科学实验需要multi-step\n    causal reasoning)。Step-independent在T=67下更catastrophic：gamma^(67-h)对任何reasonable\n    h都接近0。Episode-level仍然work(32.4%)但低于ALFWorld(48.2%)因为(1)action space更大，(2)科学实验有strict\n    causal ordering requirements，(3)1.7B model对science reasoning capacity有限。6.75x\n    improvement factor > ALFWorld的~8x（48.2/6.25），在same ballpark内confirms generalization。Step-independent完全不converge（4.8%来自random\n    success on simplest tasks like boiling water）。这addresses Reviewer Concern #2:\n    single environment。'\n  tables:\n  - title: Cross-Environment Generalization\n    columns:\n    - environment\n    - episode_level_%\n    - step_independent_%\n    - ratio\n    - mean_T\n    rows:\n    - - ALFWorld\n      - 48.2\n      - 6.0\n      - 8.0x\n      - 50\n    - - ScienceWorld\n      - 32.4\n      - 4.8\n      - 6.75x\n      - 67\n  figures_description:\n  - Side-by-side training curves for both environments, same color scheme。Pattern\n    identical：step-independent flat/collapsed, episode-level steadily improves。\n  analysis: Cross-environment validation是reviewer必问问题。6.75x improvement在不同environment\n    confirms the phenomenon is fundamental(credit assignment decay)而非environment-specific\n    artifact。Absolute success差异(48.2 vs 32.4)expected because ScienceWorld inherently\n    harder for 1.7B model，但relative advantage preserved。\n- name: 7B model scaling verification\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B\n  expected_results:\n    episode_level_7B_success: 58.7\n    step_independent_7B_success: 8.3\n    episode_level_1.7B_success: 48.2\n    step_independent_1.7B_success: 6.0\n    improvement_factor_7B: 7.07\n    improvement_factor_1.7B: 8.03\n    convergence_step_7B: 8\n    convergence_step_1.7B: 12\n  result_rationale: '7B model有更强的base capability（更好的instruction following、更大context\n    capacity），所以absolute success更高(58.7% vs 48.2%)。Step-independent在7B上略好(8.3% vs\n    6.0%)因为larger model能partially compensate credit assignment problem through better\n    in-context learning，但仍然catastrophically low。Improvement ratio略低(7.07x vs 8.03x)因为larger\n    model的stronger base means step-independent不完全collapse to 0，但差异minor。Convergence更快(8\n    vs 12 steps)因为7B的stronger initialization means fewer RL steps needed to learn\n    task policy。Key finding：episode-level advantage不因model scale减弱——it''s a fundamental\n    training methodology issue not a capacity issue。这addresses Reviewer Concern #3。'\n  tables:\n  - title: Model Scale Comparison\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - episode_level_%\n    - step_independent_%\n    - ratio\n    - convergence_step\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n      - 48.2\n      - 6.0\n      - 8.0x\n      - 12\n    - - Qwen3-7B\n      - 58.7\n      - 8.3\n      - 7.1x\n      - 8\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: 2 models × 2 methods, showing episode-level advantage preserved\n    at scale。'\n  analysis: 7B result serves dual purpose：(1)confirms advantage generalizes across\n    scale, (2)shows larger models benefit MORE in absolute terms from episode-level(+10.5pp\n    for 7B vs +42.2pp for both，but both huge). If anything，7B result makes episode-level\n    MORE important because it unlocks significantly higher absolute performance。\n- name: Per-task-type breakdown analysis\n  plan_id: plan_016\n  description: Success breakdown by ALFWorld task type with episode-length correlation\n  expected_results:\n    pick_success: 56.2\n    pick_mean_length: 22.4\n    clean_success: 48.7\n    clean_mean_length: 35.6\n    heat_success: 52.1\n    heat_mean_length: 31.2\n    cool_success: 45.3\n    cool_mean_length: 33.8\n    examine_success: 62.5\n    examine_mean_length: 18.7\n    pick_two_success: 28.4\n    pick_two_mean_length: 48.3\n    episode_length_success_correlation: -0.72\n    episode_level_advantage_vs_length_correlation: 0.61\n  result_rationale: Task difficulty与episode length高度相关(r=-0.72)。Examine最简单(62.5%)因为只需navigate+look——最短episodes(18.7步)。Pick_two最难(28.4%)因为需要两次independent\n    object interactions——最长episodes(48.3步)。Episode-level advantage与task length正相关(r=0.61)：longer\n    tasks受credit assignment问题影响更大，所以从episode-level training获益更多。Pick_two的episode-level\n    improvement最dramatic(从~3% step-independent到28.4% episode-level，~9x)而examine improvement较modest(从~10%到62.5%，~6x)。这provides\n    additional mechanistic evidence：episode-level training的benefit直接comes from solving\n    longer-horizon credit assignment。\n  tables:\n  - title: Per-Task Performance\n    columns:\n    - task_type\n    - success_%\n    - mean_episode_length\n    - episode_level_advantage_vs_step_indep\n    rows:\n    - - examine\n      - 62.5\n      - 18.7\n      - 5.2x\n    - - pick\n      - 56.2\n      - 22.4\n      - 6.8x\n    - - heat\n      - 52.1\n      - 31.2\n      - 7.9x\n    - - clean\n      - 48.7\n      - 35.6\n      - 8.3x\n    - - cool\n      - 45.3\n      - 33.8\n      - 8.1x\n    - - pick_two\n      - 28.4\n      - 48.3\n      - 9.5x\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: mean episode length (X) vs episode-level advantage ratio (Y), with\n    task type labels。Clear positive trend。'\n  - 'Stacked bar by task type: episode-level vs step-independent, sorted by episode\n    length。'\n  analysis: Per-task breakdown展示within-environment diversity并provide mechanistic validation：如果credit\n    assignment decay是root cause，那longer tasks应该show greater episode-level advantage。r=0.61确认这个prediction。这也informs\n    selective verification design：pick_two任务应receive more frequent verification because\n    they're hardest and longest。\n","numLines":919,"startLine":1,"totalLines":919}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EsQe1WykACP9qNg4j6i8Ln","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've read the paper and the review context. Now I need to dispatch a full review using the dream-review-full skill template. Let me plan the process:\n\n1. Two Reviewers: R1 (Method + Experiments) and R2 (Novelty + Related Work)\n2. Full roundtable: Step 1 (independent reviews) → Step 2 (cross-sharing) → Step 3 (convergence) → Step 4 (synthesis)\n\nLet me dispatch both reviewers in parallel as independent agents. I must NOT mention the tier (best/median/worst) or hint at result quality to the reviewers.\n\n\nNow I'm preparing comprehensive review prompts for both reviewers. The paper proposes episode-level GRPO for credit assignment in long-horizon tasks and B-IAVR selective verification using action-change as intrinsic reward, tested on ALFWorld and ScienceWorld with Qwen models achieving 48.2% success rates.\n\nLooking at the planned experiments against what's actually in the paper, I can see most of the ablations and analyses are covered—context window sweeps, multi-seed replications, credit assignment mechanisms, action-change statistics, B-IAVR training, full comparisons, no-verify ablations, and entropy-controlled analyses all appear in the tables.\n\nThe remaining experiments round out the evaluation nicely: causal interventions, reward signal ablations, ARES comparisons, ScienceWorld transfer results, 7B scaling experiments, and per-task breakdowns. This is a thorough experimental suite.\n\nNow I'm setting up R1 and R2 as parallel reviewers, each with the full paper and their specific evaluation focus.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34029,"cache_read_input_tokens":24213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34029},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3938fe37-c6ff-4c42-aa09-92ffcfd25d32","uuid":"5b3193bb-ebbe-43fe-8da9-2f3a4209933e"}
