ange rate, examine 22%\n- Entropy-controlled: partial correlation r=0.27, p=0.003 after controlling entropy\n- Causal intervention: verification-triggered 50.3% vs random 36.8% vs no-change 44.1% (p<0.001)\n\n**4.3 Selective Verification** (Tables 7-9):\n- B-IAVR training: converges step 18, verify rate 52%, 58% action-change when verified (vs 32% always-on)\n- Full comparison: B-IAVR 46.8%/52% verify. Confidence-threshold 44.3%/53%. Random 42.1%/50%. No-verify 35.6%/0%\n- Per-task: uniform degradation, max 2.3pp (pick_two)\n\n**4.4 Reward Ablation** (Table 10):\n- Action-change 46.8%, confidence-based 45.1%, task-success-only 44.8%, random-trigger 43.7%\n\n**4.5 ARES Comparison** (Table 11):\n- B-IAVR: 46.8%/52% verify/0 labels/96 GPU-h\n- ARES: 44.9%/61% verify/5000 labels/24 GPU-h\n\n**4.6 Generalization** (Table 12):\n- ScienceWorld: 32.4% vs 4.8% (6.75×)\n- Qwen3-7B: 58.7% vs 8.3% (7.1×)\n\n**4.7 Per-Task** (Table 13): advantage correlates with episode length r=0.61\n\n**4.8 No-Verify Ablation** (Table 14): 35.6% vs 48.2%, -12.6pp\n\n### Conclusion (p8-9)\nDual contribution: episode-level training + selective verification. Limitations: text-based discrete environments only; B-IAVR needs pre-converged checkpoint (96h GPU).\n\n## Experiment Design Coverage\nThe full experiment plan included 15 experiments. The paper covers all of them:\n- h-sweep ablation ✓\n- Multi-seed ✓ \n- Gradient signal mechanism ✓\n- Action-change statistics ✓\n- B-IAVR training ✓\n- Full 5-way comparison ✓\n- No-verify ablation ✓\n- Entropy-controlled analysis ✓\n- Causal intervention ✓\n- Reward signal ablation ✓\n- ARES reproduction ✓\n- ScienceWorld transfer ✓\n- 7B scaling ✓\n- Per-task breakdown ✓\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nProduce a structured review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (3-4 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (bullet points, focus on method correctness, experimental thoroughness, statistical validity)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bullet points, focus on method limitations, experimental gaps, questionable claims)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (specific, answerable)\n5. **Missing Experiments or Analysis** (what would strengthen the paper)\n6. **Minor Issues** (writing, presentation, clarity)\n7. **Preliminary Score** (1-6 with justification)\n8. **Confidence** (1-5: 1=low, 5=expert)\n\nBe rigorous. A top venue accepts ~25% of submissions. Evaluate whether this paper clears that bar.","uuid":"b6ab6479-effa-4d64-bcac-913bb668e1c4","session_id":"3938fe37-c6ff-4c42-aa09-92ffcfd25d32"}
