{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QKo3kixMh8S5pn8HVy1SrJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012eBjJSCWzFoUtugNUAbSQv","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a665580f6c49b2fd9","message":"## Step 2: Cross-Sharing\n\nRead R2's review below and prepare a brief response (under 300 words) noting:\n1. Which of R2's points you agree with\n2. Which points you disagree with and why\n3. Whether you want to adjust your score after seeing R2's perspective\n\n---\n\n## R2's Review (Novelty + Related Work focus)\n\n**Score: 3 (Weak Reject), Confidence: 4**\n\n**Novelty Assessment**: Episode-level GRPO is conceptually equivalent to REINFORCE with episode return. The gamma^(T-h) decay analysis is mathematically trivial. Action-change reward is reasonable but conceptually straightforward. B-IAVR vs Thinkless is application-level distinction, not fundamental advance.\n\n**Related Work**: Insufficient. Three paragraphs for a top venue is inadequate. Missing: GAE, hindsight credit, reward redistribution, Reflexion, SayCan, self-correction debate, process reward models, DeepSeek-R1.\n\n**Key Weaknesses**:\n- Limited novelty of episode-level GRPO (essentially REINFORCE 1992)\n- No comparison to GAE or intermediate credit assignment methods\n- \"8x improvement\" overclaims by comparing against a broken baseline\n- Only two similar text-game environments\n- B-IAVR requires 96h GPU pre-converged checkpoint\n- Related Work inadequate for top venue\n- 1.4pp gap likely not statistically significant (overlaps 2.9pp std)\n- Frozen policy assumption limits B-IAVR\n- Missing inference cost analysis\n\n**Questions**: Why not compare GAE? Can RAGEN trivially adopt episode-level by setting gamma=1? Is 1.4pp gap significant?\n\n**Missing References**: GAE (Schulman 2016), Reflexion, RUDDER, self-critical sequence training, process reward models, DeepSeek-R1."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":nul